✅ CONCLUSION

FlashCart delivers a working unified checkout for a multi-showroom mall. Customers sign in with a phone number, scan the real barcodes on product tags into one bag, and pay once by UPI, card or cash for a single GST invoice. Cashiers get a simple cash desk that shows the change to return and reconciles the drawer at the end of the day. All data is stored in SQLite, and the business rules are covered by 17 automated tests.

The biggest lessons were to test with real-world inputs (the QR scanner failed on real barcodes, and real tags include GST in the MRP), to keep the server as the only source of truth for prices and payments, and to let feedback after each iteration reshape the design.

🚀 FUTURE SCOPE
Inventory management: stock in, low-stock alerts, expiry tracking and an admin panel for products.
Hardware smart cart: a trolley with a barcode scanner or RFID reader, a Raspberry Pi / ESP32, a touchscreen and a load cell that checks weight against scanned items.
Security: SMS OTP sign-in, Razorpay webhooks, returns and refunds.
Scale: PostgreSQL, cloud deployment and a pilot in one mall wing.
